  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community based Efforts to Evaluate Intentional and Unintentional Sea Turtles Catch in Local Fisheries along the Mauritanian Coastline</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to assess directed and accidental sea turtle bycatch artisanal fisheries along the Mauritanian coast. Mauritanias 750 km coast provides rich and extensive foraging grounds for five species of sea turtles, including loggerhead sea turtles from Cape Verde nesting grounds and olive ridleys, leatherbacks and green turtles from unknown nesting populations. The intent of this project is to identify the principle fisheries and techniques with the highest level of sea turtle bycatch and to identify measures to reduce this bycatch. Activities include: 1) a questionnaire will be used to survey fisherman in coastal villages and immigrant fisherman camps to determine fishing sites, target fish, type of gear, and sea turtle bycatch, 2) onboard observers will be placed on voluntary fishing vessels to document bycatch and teach fisherman about safe handling and release techniques, and 3) work with Imraguen native fisherman to reach agreement on the use of fishing techniques that will reduce accidental captures without disturbing their traditional way of fishing.</narrative>
  </description>
